 {"id":"CF-054","title":"P4 — README status-table re-run command cannot fail: a failed node check is masked by the trailing git rev-parse, and the line depends on an export it does not carry","status":"complete","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Dogfood walk 2026-11-03 (this lane; independent re-measure at origin/main 4638e90 from a git-archive copy with a fresh HOME, and re-read at the 820e8134 tip). README.md:74 prints: home=$(mktemp -d); HOME=\"$home\" ./scripts/project-node.sh --apply --project myproject --repo https://github.com/github/gitignore --ref main; git -C \"$home/repo\" rev-parse HEAD. Two measured consequences. (1) The compound command's exit code comes from the trailing `git rev-parse HEAD`, which succeeds even when provisioning printed NODE: FAIL (2) — a user scripting the documented re-run reads rc=0 as success on a failed check, which is the exact class AGENTS.md rule 2 forbids ('a --check that cannot print FAIL is decoration'; here the FAIL prints but cannot reach the caller). (2) Executed verbatim with no prior exports it dies at layer 00 with 'FAIL crier_url — CRIER_URL unset' although the command line itself carries no CRIER_URL; the message names the fix (self-healing) but the row's own claim to be a self-contained contradiction command does not hold. No node host is needed to reproduce either leg.","acceptance_criteria":"1. The command in the README Status table, executed verbatim in a clean environment (env -i HOME=<temp> PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin), exits nonzero when the node check fails: a probe in tests/selftest.sh (or a committed transcript under docs/audits/) shows rc!=0 for the failing case and rc=0 for a passing fixture. 2. The printed command either carries the export it needs on its own line (e.g. CRIER_URL=http://crier.example:8767 prefixed) or the table states in the same cell that it requires the Quick-start exports first. 3. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip.","created_at":"2026-11-03T12:36:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T13:07:07Z","commit_hash":"d088bc6c3158ebadf32a83ec216b31c911c768ba","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"d851a4c1","ts":"2026-11-03T13:07:07Z","tree_fp":"f3825569c9c9370ea9987187e5b3e88ba8314a599f10bbb7377b0c2a24678751","artifacts":["docs/audits/code-factory-CF-054.md"]}]}}
 {"id":"CF-055","title":"P4 — project-node.sh summary count omits harness-installer failures: the child process increments its own FAILED, so NODE: FAIL (n) understates the printed FAIL rows","status":"complete","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 by the code-factory-duckbrain dogfood lane during a real node run on bunker-las-03 and re-read at tip 820e8134. scripts/project-node.sh:114-119 invokes the harness adapter as a child process (\"$inst\" --apply | --check) and never captures its exit status or row count; scripts/lib.sh:7 increments FAILED inside that child's own shell, so the parent's counter cannot see those rows. Observed: the local --check run printed 4 FAIL rows and summarised NODE: FAIL (3); the node run printed 4 parent rows plus 2 installer rows and summarised NODE: FAIL (2). The process exit code stays correct (1), so the defect is confined to the printed inventory — which is the number a user quotes and a board row records, making a node look healthier than its own transcript. Same class as AGENTS.md rule 2 (a check whose reported result does not carry the failure) and it silently corrupts any 'NODE INCOMPLETE (n)' reading.","acceptance_criteria":"1. For a run where the harness adapter prints k FAIL rows, the summary line's count equals the total number of FAIL rows printed by the run (parent rows + adapter rows); proven by a fixture in tests/selftest.sh that forces the adapter to fail and asserts the printed summary integer against grep -c '^  FAIL'. 2. That fixture can also go green: with a passing adapter the count matches and the exit code is 0. 3. Exit codes are unchanged for both cases (nonzero on any FAIL). 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip.","created_at":"2026-11-03T12:36:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T12:53:13Z","branch":"wt/cf-055","commit_hash":"bb99a5c","ci_result":"SKIP","guard_result":"PASS","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"scripts/project-node.sh:118-136 now captures the harness adapter's output to a temp file (no pipe), echoes it through unchanged, counts its '  FAIL' rows and adds them to the parent FAILED counter, so NODE: FAIL (n) equals every FAIL row the run printed. Adapter output shape and the missing-adapter FAIL row unchanged. tests/selftest.sh section 14 proves both arms: failing adapter -> 2 FAIL rows -> NODE: FAIL (2), exit 1; passing adapter -> NODE: PASS, exit 0. RED proof: the same fixture run against the pre-fix project-node.sh printed 'FAIL summary said  but the run printed 2 FAIL rows' and SELFTEST: FAIL (1). GREEN: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (14 sections). GitReins CF-055: tier1 PASS (lint/tests/secrets), tier2 PASS, verdict 20b17c27.","foreman_note":"Landed on main as bb99a5c (pushed, origin/main == bb99a5c at push). Judge ran with --scan-root into the isolated worktree /home/kara/proj-wt-cf-cf055-20261103 because the canonical checkout was being written by a sibling lane at the time; the judged tree is the pushed commit. ci_result SKIP is the documented state of this repo (no GitHub Actions workflows; gh run list returns []).","detail":{"fingerprint":"da0288bfb44ef6411281ed6b6437df0ea94870a5","evidence":[{"run_id":"bb99a5c","ts":"2026-11-03T12:53:13Z","tree_fp":"da0288bfb44ef6411281ed6b6437df0ea94870a5","artifacts":["scripts/project-node.sh","tests/selftest.sh"]}]}}
 {"id":"CF-056","title":"P4 — node-create.sh stage-2 cannot fail: four swallowed bunker calls followed by an unconditional ok staged, plus a fixed /tmp/spawn.log shared by every lane","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 on a live node (bunker-las-03) by this lane and re-read at tip 820e8134. scripts/node-create.sh:38-46 runs one mkdir exec, three `bunker cp` copies and one chmod exec, each with `>/dev/null 2>&1`, then line 48 prints ok \"staged\" \"project-node.sh + harness/install-$HARNESS.sh\" unconditionally. Nothing in the block can produce FAIL: if a copy fails (missing harness file, closed agent, full disk inside the node) the script still claims staging succeeded and the error reappears later as 'FAIL provision — node reported FAIL', which misattributes a control-host transfer failure to the node's provisioning. Second defect in the same block: the spawn log is the fixed path /tmp/spawn.log (line 35), so two lanes provisioning concurrently overwrite each other's only diagnostic, and a stale log from another lane can be printed as this run's failure. Both are AGENTS.md rule-2/rule-5 adjacent (a step that cannot fail, and a step that is not collision-safe).","acceptance_criteria":"1. A failing copy (e.g. harness adapter removed between the -x test and the cp, or a node whose target directory is read-only) produces `FAIL staged` naming the artifact that failed to land, and no `PASS provision` follows. 2. The spawn log path is unique per run (contains the agent id or a mktemp path) and is named in the failure output. 3. tests/selftest.sh carries a fixture proving the staged-failure path can go red while the happy path stays green. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip.","created_at":"2026-11-03T12:36:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T12:36:00Z"}
