 {"id":"CF-131","title":"P1 - a completion reply that echoes the task body is refused 403 GUARD_BLOCKED, so the tick never closes","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"reasoning":null,"acceptance_criteria":"1. A test asserts the dispatcher's completion payload never carries the task text (only in_reply_to, agent, ok, seconds, task_len, reply). 2. A live probe proves the same reply is accepted by the relay with the task body stripped and refused with it present, and the probe is repeatable. 3. specs/ENVELOPE.md's reserved-field section names this failure mode: the guard matches control-ish keys, so a result envelope must not carry the dispatch text. 4. A failed completion leaves the dispatch row in a state the scheduler can distinguish from running.","detail":{"fingerprint":"116bf15f7bb249ebaa3b9ee2c35b9b81ea9167811728e49eb8e9e0f7aeff9616"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:34:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T00:34:51Z"}
 {"id":"CF-132","title":"P1 - a redelivered dispatch re-executes the task; there is no idempotency key on the receive side","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"reasoning":null,"acceptance_criteria":"1. Redelivery of an already-executed message id replays the recorded result and does not start a second harness run, proven by a test that calls the handler twice with one message. 2. The ledger survives a dispatcher restart (a second process reads the prior result). 3. specs/ENVELOPE.md's idempotency clause is matched by an implementation that actually honours it. 4. An empty or non-string task is refused and acked so it cannot loop forever.","detail":{"fingerprint":"87d312eb3574407d0bd89e0a8e7aa2da227d32174804459a687c8eb0a5a0ef3a"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:34:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T00:34:55Z"}
