ara/code-factory; the probe's two written rows show repo_url matching $d/wd.\n5. The tool refuses to mutate the scheduler DB silently: --dry-run (or the default) prints the row diff and writes nothing, and a missing --prompt file exits non-zero before any write; a test covers both.\n6. Gate at the fix commit: `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS with rc 0 and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints RESULT: OK; the probe extracted from the committed board and run from the repo root exits 0 and prints the post-fix table.","detail":{"fingerprint":"fbeaa33bebdd76dcf936cdc19afda00e40148e8e6bd85ce3806a03d81f2ea93c"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:48:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T00:48:35Z","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); printf '%s\\n' 'CREATE TABLE projects (name TEXT PRIMARY KEY, repo_url TEXT, workdir TEXT, enabled INTEGER, cooldown_s INTEGER, namespace_id TEXT, parent TEXT, prompt TEXT, prompt_mode TEXT, last_tick_started TEXT, last_tick_completed TEXT, last_tick_status TEXT, consecutive_failures INTEGER, created_at TEXT, updated_at TEXT, cooldown_pin_s INTEGER, cooldown_pin_by TEXT, cooldown_pin_at TEXT, admission_mode TEXT, cooldown_floor_s INTEGER);' \"INSERT INTO projects VALUES('src-lane','local:/x/y','/x/y',1,604800,'ns','','','append','','','',0,'t','t',604800,'fleet-toml-import','2026-11-01T00:00:00Z','',0);\" \"INSERT INTO projects VALUES('live-lane','local:/x/y','/x/y',1,900,'ns','','','append','','','',0,'t','t',NULL,'','','',0);\" | sqlite3 \"$d/s.db\"; sed \"s#^DB = os.path.expanduser.*#DB = '$d/s.db'#\" scripts/clone_lane.py > \"$d/clone.py\"; python3 \"$d/clone.py\" --from src-lane --to new-lane --workdir \"$d/wd\" --namespace ns --parent p >/dev/null; echo \"clone_rc=$?\"; python3 \"$d/clone.py\" --from src-lane --to live-lane --workdir \"$d/wd\" --namespace ns --parent p >/dev/null; echo \"reconfigure_rc=$?\"; sqlite3 -header -column \"$d/s.db\" \"select name,enabled,cooldown_s,cooldown_pin_s,repo_url from projects order by name\"; rm -rf \"$d\""}
 {"id":"CF-141","title":"P4 — an adapter --check verdict counts FAIL rows only, so an UNVERIFIED harness prints PASS beside its own WARN rows (CF-106 cannot be graded from it)","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured at f49d85b with a PATH-local stub opencode that answers --version and advertises no run/exec/serve mode: `bash scripts/harness/install-opencode.sh --check` prints `WARN user_space_binary`, `WARN non_interactive`, then `OPENCODE: PASS` and exits 0 — beside its own banner line `harness: opencode (UNVERIFIED adapter)`. The summary at scripts/harness/install-opencode.sh:37 tests `$FAILED` only (same shape at install-hermes.sh:106 and install-claude-code.sh:43), so a WARN row can never affect the verdict. specs/HARNESS.md:29 says an unmeasured adapter must be marked UNVERIFIED, so `PASS` contradicts the spec status, and the PRD CF-106 cell would read this verdict as harness support. The two adapters also disagree on whether a verdict line exists at all: on this host `install-hermes.sh --check` exits 1 printing `FAIL python — hermes-agent 0.19.0 requires python >=3.11,<3.14; found 3.14.9` and no `HERMES:` line.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce on the current tree, from the repository root: the row's probe prints two `WARN` rows (`user_space_binary`, `non_interactive`), then `OPENCODE: PASS`, then `rc=0`, for a stub harness whose `--help` advertises no run/exec/serve mode — the adapter's own banner already says `UNVERIFIED adapter`.\n2. Every harness adapter's `--check` ends with one verdict line from a fixed vocabulary, decided by row counts, not by `$FAILED` alone: `PASS` only when every contract row is `PASS`; `UNVERIFIED` when at least one row is `WARN` and none is `FAIL`; `FAIL (n)` when any row is `FAIL`, with exit status nonzero. The chosen exit status for `UNVERIFIED` is stated in `specs/HARNESS.md` (spec first, per `AGENTS.md` rule 1).\n3. Three arms in `tests/selftest.sh`, each asserting the printed verdict by name